# Legacy Stack Freeze

## Context

Celery/RabbitMQ task dispatch, the Citus/ClickHouse/Redis-Sentinel data
layer, and the LGTM observability stack are not part of the
AG-UI/A2UI/A2A rewrite's scope. `worker/tasks.py`'s job is bridging Celery's
sync task context into the async agent run (`_run_coroutine_sync`) — that
bridge stays exactly as it is; only what flows through it (the event payload
shape) changes.

## Hard rules

- Don't edit Citus, ClickHouse, Redis Sentinel, monitoring, or Celery config
  as a byproduct of wiring up a new protocol.
- If a protocol requirement seems to force a change here — e.g. AG-UI needing
  a different Celery result backend, or A2A task state needing new Redis
  structures — stop and confirm with Titus before touching it. That's a
  scope-boundary decision, not an implementation detail.
- `worker/tasks.py`'s sync→async bridge (`_run_coroutine_sync`) is off-limits.
  Only the payload that flows through `run_agent_and_stream` →
  `stream_agent_events` changes shape for the new protocols; the Celery task
  mechanics do not.
